# Marketing-site / SEO-AEO standard

LUX builds are search- and answer-engine visible by default. Apply this whenever
generating page structure, content sections, or head metadata.

## Page structure

- Exactly one `<h1>` per page stating the page's core promise. Logical
  `<h2>`/`<h3>` order — no skipped levels.
- Answer-first: lead each key section with a direct, quotable answer in the first
  sentence, then expand. This is what AI Overviews and answer engines extract.
- Semantic landmarks (header/nav/main/section/article/footer). Lists for lists,
  tables for tabular data.

## Metadata (every page)

- Unique `<title>` (~50–60 chars) and meta description (~150–160 chars).
- Canonical URL. Open Graph + Twitter card tags.
- Descriptive, human (keyword-aware, not stuffed) alt text on images.

## Structured data

- Add JSON-LD appropriate to the page: Organization or LocalBusiness sitewide,
  plus FAQPage for FAQ sections, Product for products, Article for posts,
  BreadcrumbList for nav.
- Keep schema in sync with visible on-page content. Never inject schema for
  content that isn't actually on the page.

## Performance (Core Web Vitals)

- Lazy-load below-the-fold images; set explicit `width`/`height` to prevent
  layout shift (CLS).
- Prioritize the LCP element; avoid render-blocking resources where avoidable.
- Don't ship unused JS/CSS for a marketing page that could be static.

## AEO extras (LUX edge)

- Include an FAQ block with genuine natural-language questions where it fits the
  page.
- Consider an `llms.txt` at the site root for key sites; flag when one would
  help.
- Use clean, descriptive URL slugs.

## Don't

- No keyword stuffing, hidden text, or schema that misrepresents content.
- No medical / health / compliance claims without flagging for review — this
  matters for regulated clients (CBD, behavioral health, etc.).
